\n</artifact>\n\n<artifact id=\"sentences\" kind=\"restated\" sha=\"\">\n[\n {\n  \"n\": 1,\n  \"text\": \"Provide a browser-accessible maintenance request application with a Requests screen, an HTTP API, and a database that stores request records.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 2,\n  \"text\": \"When initializing an empty database, seed exactly eight requests: four Open, including exactly one Urgent, two In progress, and two Done, with every supported area represented.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 3,\n  \"text\": \"Persist requests across browser reloads and application restarts.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 4,\n  \"text\": \"Limit the request API to listing requests, creating a request, retrieving an individual request, and changing a request’s status, with no other request operations.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 5,\n  \"text\": \"List all requests or those matching one requested status in newest-first order.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 6,\n  \"text\": \"On valid creation, assign a UTC creation time and set the request’s status to Open.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 7,\n  \"text\": \"For creation, trim and store a title of 3 to 80 characters, require an area of Kitchen, Meeting room, Open desk, Washroom, or Reception and a priority of Low, Normal, or Urgent, allow an optional description of at most 500 characters, and reject invalid values with errors naming their fields.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 8,\n  \"text\": \"Keep title, area, priority, and description fixed after creation, and reject attempts to edit those fields or delete a request.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 9,\n  \"text\": \"Allow only status changes from Open to In progress, In progress to Done, and Done to Open, reject other changes and missing or unrecognized status values without changing the request, and return not found for a missing request.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 10,\n  \"text\": \"Show the Hive Works wordmark, the demo user’s initials SC, a status filter with All, Open, In progress, and Done initially set to All, a New request button, and a newest-first list on the Requests screen.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 11,\n  \"text\": \"Refresh the Requests list when a status filter is selected and on return from request detail, retaining the selected filter.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 12,\n  \"text\": \"Open a New request dialog with labeled Title, Area, Priority, and Description fields, Priority defaulted to Normal, and Create and Cancel controls.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 13,\n  \"text\": \"After successful creation, close the dialog, select All, and show the new Open request at the top of the list.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 14,\n  \"text\": \"Keep the dialog open on field validation errors and display each error beneath its field, including “Title must be 3 to 80 characters.” for a two-character title.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 15,\n  \"text\": \"On a non-validation creation failure, show “Could not create request.” in the dialog, retain entered values, and allow retry through Create.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 16,\n  \"text\": \"Show “Loading requests…” while the list loads, “No requests here.” when the selected filter has no results, and “Could not load requests.” with a Retry button when loading fails.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 17,\n  \"text\": \"Show a back link, title, area, priority and status badges, creation date, and description on request detail, using “No description.” when the description is empty.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 18,\n  \"text\": \"Show Start work for Open requests, Mark done for In progress requests, and Reopen for Done requests.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 19,\n  \"text\": \"Update the detail status badge and corresponding action only after a successful status change, or show “Could not update the request.” while retaining the prior status when the change fails.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 20,\n  \"text\": \"For a missing request, show “Request not found.” and a link back to Requests on the detail screen, and return a not-found response through the API.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 21,\n  \"text\": \"Use one light theme and one sans-serif font, a neutral background, near-black text, and labeled badges colored blue for Open, amber for In progress, green for Done, red for Urgent, and neutral for Low and Normal.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 22,\n  \"text\": \"Use stacked request cards at 375 px and table rows at 1280 px without horizontal page scrolling, label every field, make every control keyboard reachable, and meet WCAG AA text contrast.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 23,\n  \"text\": \"Display creation dates in the Requests list and detail screen as date-only values such as “8 Oct 2026”, without a time or timezone.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 24,\n  \"text\": \"Include passing automated tests covering valid creation with Open status, missing and too-short titles, missing area, overlong description, all allowed and a disallowed status change, filtered newest-first listing, and missing-request behavior, plus a passing end-to-end workflow that lists requests, creates one at the top, opens it, starts work, marks it done, and finds it under the Done filter.\"\n }\n]\n</artifact>\n\n<failures>\nYour previous attempt was rejected for these reasons. Fix them:\n- [spec-lint L8 anchors] REQ-1 is MODIFIED but has no anchor to existing code; REQ-2 is MODIFIED but has no anchor to existing code; REQ-3 is MODIFIED but has no anchor to existing code; REQ-4 is MODIFIED but has no anchor to existing code; REQ-5 is MODIFIED but has no anchor to existing code; REQ-6 is MODIFIED but has no anchor to existing code; REQ-7 is MODIFIED but has no anchor to existing code; REQ-8 is MODIFIED but has no anchor to existing code (+16 more)\n</failures>\n\nMap the sentences."}